note:
R137 - gen7 venue packages (`rendering/stadium/stadium_<artid>_container_<n>.rx2|.rpsgl`): writer-boundary measurements for a same-size,
same-format raster replacement (research package 4, 28 Sep 2026). Read-only on the installed trees.
Per package (X360 NHL 10 / 13 / 15 / Legacy, PS3 NHL 15 / Legacy - the R127f trees):
  S1 file table: every entry's absolute span (0x10031 data = hdr_size + offset; others absolute), pairwise overlaps, data-region coverage;
  S2 X360 descriptors (0x20003, 0x40 B used): DW0, format byte, dims (DW2), pitch (DW0 bits 22-30 x 32), DW8 entry, mip count (byte 54),
     DW12 mip page (u32 @48 >> 12, x 4096), the Studio-model tiled base size, entry size; descriptors per DW8 entry (sharing);
     Studio's audited large-level gate by form (DXT1/3/5, both axes 256-1024, DW0 0x00400003, >= 2 levels, entry < 6 chains);
  S3 PS3 descriptors (0x38 B): signature u16 @34/38/42, dims u16 @48/50, mips u8 @52; search for the descriptor field that names the
     pixel entry (each u32 / u16 position vs 0x10031 entry indices whose size equals the plain chain for the format candidate
     83f1 -> 8 B blocks, 83f2 / 83f3 -> 16 B, 6007 -> 4 B texels; one-block floor per level);
  S4 board-ad descriptors (R127f slot rule: u32 @+256 of the 0xEF0001 chunk before each `adbd_*` / `BoardAd_plastic_mat*` 0xEF0005
     material): materials per descriptor (a replacement changes every material that points at it);
  S5 integrity words: CRC-32 / Adler-32 / FNV-1a-32 of the whole file, the data region, and every 0x10031 entry, looked up among every u32
     of the header, file table and non-pixel entries (bounded - other algorithms / fields untested);
  S6 X360 vs PS3 same-art check (Legacy stadium_1 and stadium_20 board-ad rasters by material name): X360 base level untiled
     (XGAddress2DTiledOffset, R66) and 16-bit byte-swapped vs the PS3 entry's first base-level bytes;
  S7 loose / archive aliases: every `rendering/stadium/` member of the tree's EB archives unwrapped (chunklzx / chunkzip) and compared with
     the loose file; BIG4 trees: names only.
Usage: python r137_venue_package_writer_boundaries.py <out.json> [--trees x360-legacy,...] [--max-per-tree N]
